Expert AI: lazy cloning in simulateAction
=========================================

Salvaged from the abandoned worktree .claude/worktrees/perf-expert-ai-lazy-clone
on 2026-07-31. The work was never committed; the worktree's branch
(worktree-perf-expert-ai-lazy-clone) held no commits of its own and has been
deleted. Base commit: 0a7cb54 (2026-06-18).

What it does
------------
simulateAction cloned all four SimState maps for every candidate action. This
copies only the maps the action actually mutates: tileMap (~150 entries on a
full board) and balances are cloned for captures only, since repositions,
builds and upgrades never touch them. The author's own estimate was 4-6x less
allocation per candidate, which matters most late-game where Expert's cost
scales with owned territory and the eval loop dominates.

Do NOT git apply this blindly
-----------------------------
aiExpert.ts has moved on since the base commit (88ee106, 452b136 at minimum).
Read it as a design sketch and re-implement against the current file. The
correctness-critical detail it gets right: on a capture, the UNMUTATED s0.tileMap
and s0.entities serve as the previousTileMap/prevEntities snapshots that
recalculateTerritoriesForCapture needs — that is what makes skipping the clone
safe, and any re-implementation has to preserve it.

Verify any re-implementation with a seeded self-play A/B (new vs old), not
against Hard, which is saturated.

